[instrumental]

[Intro - Fanfare, maestoso ~60 BPM]
[bold declarative synth-brass fanfare, forte, stacked DX7 brass stabs with quick triplet flourishes, cymbal swell rising underneath]
[fanfare surges faster, then melts away soft, one warm chord left hanging in the air]

[The Gift Theme - gently, ~92 BPM]
[tender melody on bell-toned DX7 electric piano like a music box, soft vibraphone patch doubling the tune]
[each phrase arcs gently upward and settles back on a long note, warm pad chords breathing underneath, innocent and unhurried]
[muted synth lead echoes the melody quietly, tiny sixteenth-note mallet ripples answering below]

[Gyzmo - vivace ~160 BPM, playful]
[quick skipping melody on bright bell synth, staccato repeated eighth-note pulse chattering underneath like circuit switches flipping in the walls]
[low oscillator bassline staccato like tiny gremlin footsteps on hardwood, triangle dings, everything light on its toes, mischief still innocent]

[Grand Pause]
[one full bar of dead silence, everyone holds their breath]

[The Gift - reprise, gently ~92 BPM]
[warm flugelhorn-like synth lead restates the tender theme softer than before, morphoder warble creeping in at the edges like a bad mogwai testing the air]
[triplet figures begin to stir, accelerando, crescendo, cymbal roll rising - the mischief hatches]

[Main Theme - The Hook, allegro ~120 BPM]
[the famous hook arrives sempre forte, bells doubling the melody on DX7, oom-pah synth bass strutting, cabasa and drum set swinging]
[the hook is VOCAL: the synth lead runs through a vocoder-talkbox morphoder so every note has a mouthy formant shape, like a chorus of bad mogwai chanting the riff themselves - do do do do do do BEAT]
[hook phrase one: a chain of quick even staccato notes chattering on one pitch, peppy and relentless, an accent leaning on the end of the run, then dropping onto one short punchy landing note - the BEAT]
[hook phrase two: the same chattering run again, note for note, cockier, landing on its beat]
[hook phrase three: the run doubles in length - stair-stepping eighth notes climbing the scale with off-beat accents, twice as many little voices - do do do do do do do do do do BEAT - tumbling onto accented hits with grace-note flicks, cowbell on the landing]
[whole hook restated with thicker synth stabs behind it, accents popping, chaotic but tight as a drum]

[Second Strain - smoother]
[legato singing line slides over the oom-pah bass, sly and slinky, accompaniment still detached and precise underneath]
[the hook cell sneaks back in with accents, trading between high oscillator lead and answering voices, cowbell punctuation]

[Low Strain - marcato]
[melody drops into the bass synths with heavy marcato swagger, snare rattling sixteenth notes, china cymbal crashes like pans falling in the kitchen]

[Breakdown - gremlin cackle]
[flutter-tongued growling synth chatter like gremlins laughing inside the walls, morphoder warble on every note, dying away to almost nothing]

[Quiet Restart - long build]
[the hook whispered pianissimo over tiptoeing oom-pah bass, drum set feather-light, then a long patient crescendo as voices stack one by one]

[Full Chorus - key lifts]
[whole band slams back in forte, ride cymbal driving, the hook shifted up a half step, brighter and more unhinged than before]

[Finale]
[final strain hammering the hook, sforzando swell blooming, xylophone flourish flashing like firecrackers]
[stinger: sharp accented full-band hits, then one beat of silence]
[final declarative cowbell hit rings out into the dark, tip your synth programmer]
